Changes applied to DCP (https://github.com/chenyu-jiang/dcp) @ e1e19b8 for the evaluation:
- DCP_FP32_OUT=1: forward partial outputs and backward partial dQ / dK / dV stored, sent and reduced in fp32 (the
  kernels write fp16 scratch rows that are widened); the planner prices those blocks at 4 bytes per element.
- Communication / compute cost model of the target cluster from the environment: DCP_INTER_GBPS, DCP_INTRA_GBPS,
  DCP_INTER_LAT_MS, DCP_INTRA_LAT_MS, DCP_PEAK_TFLOPS, DCP_PEAK_MEMBW (unset: upstream defaults).
- DCP_SMALL_SMEM=1 (default): the 32-token reduction tile for GPUs with ~100 KB shared memory per block.
- Microbenchmark: mask type 'ranges_file' (two key ranges per token from DCP_RANGES_FILE), per-rank plan cache
  (DCP_PLAN_CACHE), latency mode (DCP_BENCH_LATENCY=1: barrier before every call, slowest rank, median of 10).

